 "result_text": "I fixed the `IndexError` when `icr_custom_value` is 0. I haven't run any tests or the reproduction.\n\n`LUX_MAPPING_VALUES` had 10 entries, but `icr_custom_value` can be 0 to 10. A value of 0 looked up index `10 - 0 = 10`, which is out of range. I made two changes:\n\n- **Lux table:** I appended `0` to `LUX_MAPPING_VALUES` in `src/uiprotect/data/devices.py`. A custom value of 0 now shows as 0 lux (\"under 1 lux\").\n- **Lux range:** I changed `ICRLuxValue` in `src/uiprotect/data/types.py` from `ge = 1` to `ge = 0`. This lets `set_icr_custom_lux(0)` be used. It maps to a custom value of 0, which matches the new table entry.\n\nMy first edit hit the wrong line in `devices.py`, so I reverted that file and redid it. The diff above is the final state.",
